# Vue 3 Frontend

## Feature Structure

```text
features/{name}/
  api/          Thin httpClient wrappers (one function per endpoint)
  composables/  State + orchestration (return Result<T>)
  model/        Types, schemas, pure domain helpers
  components/   Feature UI (presentational)
pages/          Route views — thin orchestrators only
shared/         httpClient, Base* inputs, utilities
```

## Component Patterns

- Always `<script setup lang="ts">` — no Options API
- Typed `defineProps` / `defineEmits`; emit events up, never mutate props
- Shared form components use `modelValue` + `update:modelValue`
- Reuse `BaseInput`, `BaseTextarea`, `BaseNumberInput`, `BaseSelect`

## State & API

- Cross-route state: module-level singleton composables (see `useSession`)
- HTTP only via `shared/api/httpClient.ts` — feature `api/` modules are thin wrappers
- Configure auth once: `httpClient.configure({ tokenProvider, workspaceProvider })`
- Gym-scoped calls: `{ auth: true, workspace: true }`

## Data Mapping

- UI form types in `model/wodTypes.ts` (discriminated unions for config)
- API ↔ form mapping in `model/wodSchemas.ts` (`detailToFormState`, `stageToPayload`)
- Permission checks as pure functions: `canCreateWOD()`, `canEditWOD()`

## Styling

- **No** `<style scoped>` blocks — global CSS in `src/styles/` + `style.css`
- Use CSS custom properties from `tokens.css`; theme via `[data-theme='light'|'dark']`
- Badge/class mapping in TS (`wodTheme.ts`) → CSS classes like `badge-amrap`

## TypeScript

- Strict mode; `@/` imports; `import type` for types
- Use `Result<T>` — check `.ok` before accessing `.value`
- No `any`; prefer discriminated unions over loose objects

## Router

- Guards in `app/router.ts` using `useSession()` — no inline fetch in guards
- Pages handle loading/error UI; composables return `Result<T>`
